{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/791822-solar-survival-at-essence-4-5","id":791822,"title":"Solar Survival at Essence 4&5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-23T15:36:36-08:00","id":791822,"title":"Solar Survival at Essence 4&5?","content":"So, the Solar Survival Charms in the Core only go up to Essence 3. Note that I am not complaining about this. Deadly Predator Method scares the crap out of me and (especially once you can apply such things to an Elemental/Demonic Familiar) and there are plenty of charms to grab before you can get it.<br /> <br /> What I AM wondering about is... Well, where do you go from here? Deadly Predator Method is pretty crazy and, while I didn't read the charms in detail, it looks like all the bases are covered. It doesn't seem like we necessarily even need higher essence charms here. I suppose that granting your familiar Legendary Size might be E4, but I dunno.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Am I way off base? Is there some stuff you want that is very obviously E4 or E5? Vance, do you have any thoughts about where you'd like to go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T16:32:49-08:00","id":791846,"title":"","content":"Essence 3 is, as you noticed, where a lot of the realultimatepower of Solar Charms lives.<br /> <br /> Once you reach Essence 4, the Charms you find tend more towards a couple of things:<br /> \u2022 Raw power tends to be channeled towards into a specific condition, circumstance, or restriction, as opposed to the more broadly applicable power you find in Essence 3 Charms., e.g. Flashing Nocturne Prana, Heavens Crash Down, Inviolable Essence-Merging, Subject-Hailing Ideology<br /> \u2022 Providing upgrades or extensions the Charms you've been using so far, e.g. Bonfire Anima Wings, Dust and Ash Sleight, Seal of Infinite Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Essence 5 opens the gates to new worlds of possibility through powerful apex Charms that define and reinforce archetypes that exist in the Ability. They tend to provide the finishing touches for some character concepts fresh out of chargen through Supernal Abilities. Nine Aeons Thew, for instance, increases the scale of what you can achieve with feats of strength to bounds of conceptual possibility, defining the mythic strength of Herakles; Living Wind Approach lets Hermes/Atlanta/Hiawatha outspeed Mercury (uh, the Maiden) in a foot race.<br /> <br /> (usual caveats: not a dev, didn't write the Solar Charms)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 12-23-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T17:02:12-08:00","id":791856,"title":"","content":"I could imagine an E4 or E5 Survival Charm that grants your Familiar a sort of immortality. Not necessarily a mechanical unkillability (DPM has that covered) but a narrative persistence. Maybe something along the lines of a permanent spirit-bond such that the Familiar's essence finds its way back into the world and to the Solar through any adversity or barrier, even death - though perhaps not unchanged from the journey.<br /> <br /> Perhaps other beings that share its nature intuitively recognize this bond and defer to it, allowing the Familiar to command others of its kind the way Solars rule nations. Your tiger Familiar is now a prince among the world's felines! You may now take social influence actions through your pet and even command armies of cats to pounce upon your enemies!<br /> <br /> ...that got a little sillier than I expected it to. Oh well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T17:28:06-08:00","id":791864,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... If we're going for mythic resonance at E5, then would that perhaps turn a familiar into a Legendary Animal? Legend Beast Saga and Deadly Predator Method are both very awesome, true, but neither is always on. Would E5 be for things like &quot;My Housecat is now the Nemean Lion&quot; at all times? I suppose, mechanically, that would turn the familiar into a Behemoth or something, which I'm not 100% sure should be in the Solar's wheelhouse. Perhaps something that lets them tame behemoths (assuming they can't already anyway)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T18:26:07-08:00","id":791888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/791822-solar-survival-at-essence-4-5?p=791864#post791864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... If we're going for mythic resonance at E5, then would that perhaps turn a familiar into a Legendary Animal? Legend Beast Saga and Deadly Predator Method are both very awesome, true, but neither is always on. Would E5 be for things like &quot;My Housecat is now the Nemean Lion&quot; at all times?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best answer I could come up with means it depends on how you define legendary.&quot; Taking a powerful Charm with a limited duration, and give it an Essence 5 upgrade that makes it essentially constant is enough to catch my mental red flags for &quot;I should test this a bunch before I send it to the devs.&quot;<br /> <br /> A useful perspective is that of a player at character creation. If you've already sunk the majority of your initial Charm choices into picking up Deadly Predator Method, being able to use your last pick or a couple of BP to become just plain <i>better</i> than using Deadly Predator Method on its own tends to warp progression towards conformity (i.e. one true builds), rather than rewarding specific choices that player makes. This isn't necessarily broken (and homebrew is so much more forgiving of broken stuff), but that's something that would push me towards Essence 3 when I decide the Charm's minimum.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Essence minimums are a much easier place to finish your Charms than to begin them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T18:32:29-08:00","id":791892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/791822-solar-survival-at-essence-4-5?p=791864#post791864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;My Housecat is now the Nemean Lion&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And thus He-Man and Battle-cat entered the world of Exalted...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T18:38:57-08:00","id":791897,"title":"","content":"How about a charm that lets you loan or give your familiars away, with upgrades allowing them to keep some of the essence-fueled prowess that is no longer available to them in your absence?<br /> <br /> It is one thing to encounter Phaerus, Master of Hounds, and another thing for his every friend and ally to be guarded by one of the legendary Phaeron Hounds, who are said to smell ill intent from miles away and to be a match in pitched battle against a hundred men. This turns Solar Survival, late-game, into a narrative force not unlike Solar War. You can share your strength with Creation by training its guardians, rather than having to be everywhere, personally.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is where tyrant lizards come from, in my next game. Some frustrated first age zenith got tired of his worshipers dying every time he went on a wyld bender, so he invented dinosaurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T21:55:23-08:00","id":791973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/791822-solar-survival-at-essence-4-5?p=791888#post791888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best answer I could come up with means it depends on how you define legendary.&quot; Taking a powerful Charm with a limited duration, and give it an Essence 5 upgrade that makes it essentially constant is enough to catch my mental red flags for &quot;I should test this a bunch before I send it to the devs.&quot;<br /> <br /> A useful perspective is that of a player at character creation. If you've already sunk the majority of your initial Charm choices into picking up Deadly Predator Method, being able to use your last pick or a couple of BP to become just plain <i>better</i> than using Deadly Predator Method on its own tends to warp progression towards conformity (i.e. one true builds), rather than rewarding specific choices that player makes. This isn't necessarily broken (and homebrew is so much more forgiving of broken stuff), but that's something that would push me towards Essence 3 when I decide the Charm's minimum.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Essence minimums are a much easier place to finish your Charms than to begin them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, granted. In this particular case, I was thinking about Monsters from actual Legends, like the Nemean Lion, the Hydra, the Sphinx. Creatures that were notable for having this one nigh-perfect legendary thing they did. I feel like granting a power like that to my Familiar might need to be up there a bit in Essence (even if it only triggers while SBV or DPM are active).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T23:14:38-08:00","id":792004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/791822-solar-survival-at-essence-4-5?p=791892#post791892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And thus He-Man and Battle-cat entered the world of Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition had battlecat. he was called Proto Puma Prime","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T23:25:30-08:00","id":792011,"title":"","content":"Isn't Saga Beast Virtue already the Charm that turns Cringer into Battle Cat?<br /> <br /> I wonder if He-Man is a Dawn or a Zenith. On the one hand, he doesn't really do much other than fight and look super ultramasculine. On the other hand, I really want to give him more Survival Charms at Essence 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T05:27:44-08:00","id":792111,"title":"","content":"I feel as if the blond pageboy kind of gets in the way of looking super ultramasculine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:16:57-08:00","id":792291,"title":"","content":"What about training a familiar in ways beyond what an animal can normally learn, such as speech and intelligence? Fully awakening the animal? Training the familiar such that it can train other animals of the same type and issue commands as a leader of a battlegroup? <br /> <br /> For other aspects of survival, what about charms that make an already hostile environment more hostile? Actively hide sources of water in the desert? Or a charm that prevents someone else from using a resource by consuming it or packing it up or taking it with you (like an oasis)?<br /> <br /> These are mostly unrefined ideas I am spitballing here, but some might have what you are looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:31:12-08:00","id":792389,"title":"","content":"A pinnacle Essence 5 Survival charm should allow the character to describe exactly what a Lunar is in a single sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3752-mushroom-king","name":"Mushroom King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:45:32-08:00","id":792397,"title":"","content":"Kinda out there, possibly outside of the Solar themes, but perhaps something branching off of Element Resisting Prana that allows the Solar &quot;become one with their environment&quot;, subsuming themselves within it, effectively ceasing to be for a while, thus not needing food, water, et cetera, as well as avoiding being located, or attacked (except by massive area attacks, I guess)?<br /> <br /> Maybe with a further upgrade that allows the Solar some extra geomantic tricks when subsuming themselves within a Demense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}